WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:06.640
What if you’re an airline and you want to sell&nbsp;
110 tickets… but your plane only has 100 seats?&nbsp;

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.560
Sounds like you can’t do that, right?
Well, you can.&nbsp;

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:15.040
What airlines do is intentionally&nbsp;
overbook flights because they know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:21.280
statistically, some passengers won’t show up.
So instead of letting empty seats fly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:27.280
they sell more tickets than seats.
Now, what if everybody shows up?&nbsp;

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:31.120
Well, they got a problem.
What they’ll usually do is ask for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:37.520
volunteers to take a later flight in exchange for&nbsp;
cash, vouchers, or other forms of compensation.&nbsp;

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:41.929
Overbooking a really quick and easy&nbsp;
way for airlines to make more money.

